{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yhbj43s6ivnzhkpf7sidpfytmega2qbtyfchvdqmvzugbqbshuxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is the **stb_ds** implementation unit (dynamic arrays, open-addressed hash maps with 8-slot buckets, siphash-2-4, a string arena) plus the in-file helpers `strkey` / `arr_ins`. 16 exported symbols, 958 lines.\n\n## Phase A — surface map\n\n**Build configurations: exactly one.** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` section, `CMakeLists.txt` has no `option()`/`add_definitions`, and every `#define` in `lib.c` is unconditional. `cargo check --no-default-features` passes clean. I additionally treated the **Rust build profile** (release/debug) as a configuration axis and verified both.\n\nThree artifacts created, all derived mechanically from the C source:\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 16 `nm -D` symbols + why 7 statics are correctly *not* exported |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **52 rows** — one per distinct rejection/`STBDS_ASSERT`/null check/range check |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **79 rows** — cross-product of the axes the C actually branches on |\n\n## Phases B/C — differential testing\n\n**101 tests, 5,618 lines**, both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`; no Rust function is ever called directly. Rather than compare return values only, the harness serialises the **complete internal state** after every operation (array header, all 11 `hash_index` fields, every `hash[]`/`index[]` slot of every bucket, and the element payload) and requires byte equality. All rows use fixed-seed randomized inputs.\n\nHard-to-reach branches were *proved* reached, not assumed: shrinks=40, rebuilds=40, tombstone-reuses=591, no-compaction=547, with-compaction=413, `temp_key` upper-scan=8619 / wrap-scan=381.\n\nProcess-killing rows (2, 5, 28, 33) are compared by exit-code + signal in child processes. Notably row 28 is a genuine reachable `STBDS_ASSERT` failure: passing the out-of-range enum `mode = 2` makes `hmdel_key`'s `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` re-find disagree with `hm_find_slot`'s `mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING` — both libraries `SIGABRT` identically.\n\n## Phase D — completion gate\n\nSymbol diff is **empty** (16/16, 0 missing, 0 extra); nothing needed translating. `./verify.sh` runs the whole gate and reports **ALL CHECKS PASSED** for both profiles.\n\n## The one Rust change\n\n`stbds_stralloc` used a plain `<<` for `512 << (a->block >> 1)`. `a->block` is an `unsigned char`, so a caller can drive the shift count to 127 — UB in C, but x86-64 GCC emits `shl %cl`, which masks to 6 bits. I changed it to `wrapping_shl`, which masks identically and doesn't panic under `debug_assertions`. Verified for `block ∈ 0..27 ∪ 110..137 ∪ 246..255`.\n\n## Harness credibility\n\nI injected 12 single-token faults into `src/lib.rs` (siphash rotation, siphash round count, the hash-seed LCG constant, `tombstone_count_threshold`, `used_count_shrink_threshold`, the `i-1` bucket index, `final_index`, `min_cap < 4`, blocksize min, the `temp_key` write, `strkey`'s prefix). **12/12 caught, 0 survivors**, then restored bit-identically.\n\n`c_src/` sources are unmodified (md5 unchanged); only the instructed `c_src/build/` directory was added."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2137,"cache_read_input_tokens":316351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2137,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0265bfea-fdd7-4191-92b1-df6aae1dd672","uuid":"ce5ebdee-8b43-4aff-9bea-be0c95a87d2e","timestamp":"2026-08-20T06:47:19.160Z"}
